t{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\n\nWe use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}_{m},{y}_{m}) & =(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{-3a+3a}{2},\\frac{6b+8b}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{0}{2},\\frac{14b}{2}) \\\\  & =(0,7b)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186074071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073714 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "58e2e40e-209b-5bc7-98df-11841c2bbcc3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Midpoint of a Segment With Variable Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "eee5b7ab-c133-57eb-9614-aeff1522c54c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070332} {:answer-field/id #uuid "5e65decf-258e-5566-95ef-5b3bd98f8cc1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186070333}] :question/id #uuid "da9fefdc-bf24-5050-9662-b6463d7dc33f" :question/math-academy-id "q-216932" :question/problem "The midpoint of the line segment with endpoints $(a, 2b)$ and $(5a, 7b)$\nis$($\n{{field-1}}\n$$,\n{{field-2}}\n$)$."}]}
